<title>USA: USDA's Drazek - WTO beef hormone panel went well.</title>
<headline>USDA's Drazek - WTO beef hormone panel went well.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department senior trade adviser Paul Drazek said the first day of hearings by a World Trade Organization panel on the U.S. complaint over the EU ban on hormone-treated beef went well.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it went very well, but in any case they're confidential and we're really not at liberty to discuss the proceedings,&quot; Drazek told USDA Radio in a telephone interview from Geneva on Thursday after the hearing.</p>
<p>Drazek said the panel will meet again in about a month.</p>
<p>The U.S. opposes the EU hormone ban, in place since 1989, arguing it is not based on any scientific justification.</p>
<p>&quot;We have wealth of supporting material and we have a wealth of scientific information on our side and that's why we continue to be confident of ultimate victory,&quot; Drazek said in the radio interview.</p>
</text>
